<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48278" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεο-πρόπος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>prophetic</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰωνιστής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					13.70
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					822
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦτορ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					12.534
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Subst., <i>seer, prophet</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.228
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.416
			</span></i>; of <i><span class="en">
				Moses
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.199
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοπρόπον, τό</span>,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεοπροπία</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Lav. Pall.</u>
				125
			</span></i>(pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>public messenger sent to inquire of an oracle</i>, 
				Ion.
			 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρός</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.48
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				659
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).141.9
			</span></i> (Paros, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				548.2
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cim.</u>
				18
			</span></i>: pl., as pr. n. of a family (= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θεοπροπίδαι</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				2.125
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				2.9
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-προπο-</span> assim. fr.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-προκο-</span>, cf. Lat. <i>procus,
				precor.</i>)</div>
